{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 12, :comments ["<b>And you shall set bounds, etc.</b> It appears that the commandment of this demarcation applies only to the third day; nevertheless He stated it from now on so that they would treat it with honor from this moment, and also accustom themselves to keep away from it during the three days. Nor should one say that the prohibition of touching the mountain should take effect from the day of its command — this is not so, for it is a remote thing that the mountain should become sanctified and incur liability upon it before the descent of His Shekhinah, blessed be He. And so it follows from the Mishnah in Sifrei (Mekhilta 24), that the prohibition did not begin until the third day."], :book :exodus, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 19, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:30:11.247213201Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}